30,2,1,talk,Servas,,It seems hardware and physical assets bring transparency but add significant delays and costs to our audits. We must weigh this carefully.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings suggest that back-office financial tools have been our most successful exits, while operational businesses with physical premises have failed us.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Minako,,"We are spending follow-on capital far too quickly on equipment-heavy holdings. Furthermore, our credit line is useless for software-based security.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh no! It looks like we are totally overloaded with software board seats, and we can't find people for physical operations quickly at all!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Toshio,,I've found that medical records and financial data cause massive deployment delays. Hardware is also prone to supply chain failures.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, so software isn't necessarily faster if it involves sensitive data?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, if the credit line doesn't support subscriptions, we must be cautious about the burn rate of software companies.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Exactly, Asuka. We need a balance. We cannot afford more unexpected capital calls for hardware, nor can we rely on a credit line that ignores our software assets.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Mio,,But we can't take on more software if the partners are already doing eleven board seats! We'll be too tired!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Toshio,,The most reliable delivery I saw was a bank tool. It avoided both the security lag of medical data and the shortages of hardware.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Mio, your point on capacity is valid. However, the transparency of physical assets is a comfort during the quarter-end stress.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Asuka,,Transparency is useless if the business model fails. The write-off was a physical operation. The wins were financial tooling.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I must prioritize the fund's solvency. Hardware is draining our reserves faster than planned. I lean toward software, provided it isn't too complex.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Mio,,I just don't want us to spend all our time recruiting for field crews that never show up!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we want to avoid ""obstacles outside the team's hands,"" we should avoid hardware and medical security reviews.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Servas,,It seems we are torn between the audit ease of software and the verification ease of hardware.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"The data on retention is clear: independent practices and field instruments are stable, but shopkeeper tools are not.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Minako,,We need a candidate that doesn't trigger early follow-on calls for equipment.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Mio,,Let's just pick something that doesn't make us do more board work or impossible hiring!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for the path of least resistance regarding deployment and delivery.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
